    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.operators / multiply operator\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nA common operation I do when refactoring or whatever  is copying some piece of code, pasting it then commenting the original piece of code.\r\n\r\nSo one could for example go from `{foo=\"bar\"}` to\r\n ```lua\r\n-- {foo=\"bar\"}\r\n{foo = \"bar\"}\r\n```\r\njust with `gmm` rather than duplicating then going back to the original piece of code, commenting, then going all the way down to the duplicated piece of code to modify it, which takes significantly more time outside of this trivial example. \r\n\r\nIs it possible to do something like that ? \r\n\r\n",
