            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the question/suggestion!\r\n\r\nI am encountering this quite often myself. Yet still not sure if there is a proper/good way to make this experience better from inside 'mini.operators' itself.\r\n\r\nWhat I'd suggest to do right now is to make custom mappings. For example in the issue it is quite straightforward:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', 'gmc', 'gmmkgccj', { remap = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor action on visual selection - not so much, but still doable. For full operator - not so much, as it should take a motion/textobject after itself.\r\n\r\nI'll take a closer look, but not sure this will be made better in 'mini.operators' itself.",
