        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "So after thinking about it, I indeed don't think there is a good design to be had in 'mini.operators' itself to allow this \"comment after multiply\" action/mappings.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nThat said, there is a `MiniOperators.config.multiply.func` which can be used to execute any action *before* multiplication is maid. With some dark Neovim magic of `vim.cmd()` and `vim.schedule()`, there is a (kind of) solution that looks like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal schedule_comment = function()\r\n  local cur_line = vim.fn.line('.')\r\n  vim.schedule(function()\r\n    -- Comment multipled text (assumes `gc` as comment operator)\r\n    vim.cmd(\"normal '[gc']\")\r\n    -- Put cursor on initial line on first non-blank character\r\n    vim.api.nvim_win_set_cursor(0, { cur_line, 0 })\r\n    vim.cmd(\"normal! ^\")\r\n  end)\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal multiply_and_comment = function()\r\n  local cur_multiply_func = MiniOperators.config.multiply.func\r\n  MiniOperators.config.multiply.func = function(content)\r\n    -- Comment multiplied lines (and only lines)\r\n    if content.submode == 'V' then schedule_comment() end\r\n    return content.lines\r\n  end\r\n  vim.schedule(function() MiniOperators.config.multiply.func = cur_multiply_func end)\r\n  return 'gm'\r\nend\r\n\r\nvim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x' }, 'gmc', multiply_and_comment, { expr = true, remap = true })\r\n```\r\n\r\nNow something like `gmc` followed by `ip` will comment multiplied inner paragraph (to be put *after* current inner paragraph, as any multiplied text) and put cursor on the first non-blank line. It is not 100% perfect (relies on `gc` being commenting operator, there might be some flicker, and in Visual mode it needs to wait 'timeoutlen' to make sure that `gm` mapping should be executed), but it works.",
